WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:07.920
Hey, David, if Joe Biden manages to win Florida
back from Trump, is it over for Donald Trump?

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.300
So I understand why people are asking this.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.200
Florida is a big prize electorally.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.170
It's 29 electoral votes.

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:19.590
And right now, Joe Biden is leading by an
average of six point four in Florida.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:24.900
That's a range of anywhere from being tied
in Florida to Biden, plus 10 in Florida.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:29.380
The real Clear Politics average in Florida
right now is that Biden is up by six point

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.410
four.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:33.480
So let's start with just the simple mathematical
case.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:38.670
If you start with the 2016 map where Trump
won Florida and the only change you make is

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:41.230
you flip Florida to Biden.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:43.870
That is not enough for Joe Biden to win the
presidency.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:48.750
Biden winning Florida and otherwise, the map
staying is 27.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:52.379
2016 would give Trump 277 still.

00:00:52.379 --> 00:00:54.580
You only need 270 to be president.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:58.829
So Florida alone will not help Joe Biden win.

00:00:58.829 --> 00:01:00.160
However.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:07.630
These elections rarely are completely isolated,
where everything is the same as 2016 except

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:13.930
one state flips, if Biden wins Florida, he
probably is going to win something else.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:19.450
Like, for example, Wisconsin, Michigan or
Pennsylvania.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:24.639
If Biden wins Florida back and Wisconsin,
he wins.

00:01:24.639 --> 00:01:28.869
If Biden wins Florida, back in Michigan, he
wins.

00:01:28.869 --> 00:01:33.459
If Biden wins Florida and Pennsylvania back,
he also wins.

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:40.899
And even if Trump holds Florida, so Trump
keeps Florida and keeps Ohio, Biden can still

00:01:40.899 --> 00:01:46.329
win by winning any two of the three states,
Wisconsin, Michigan and Pennsylvania.

00:01:46.329 --> 00:01:50.520
Now, of course, there's other opportunities
for Joe Biden as well.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:53.889
Arizona is very much in play for Joe Biden.

00:01:53.889 --> 00:01:56.130
North Carolina is close.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:02:02.719
So in the mathematical sense alone, Florida
only will not do it for Joe Biden.

00:02:02.719 --> 00:02:08.759
My belief is that if we see Joe Biden win
in Florida, he will certainly win some other

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:10.679
state that I mentioned.

00:02:10.679 --> 00:02:14.500
There's almost an exact analysis to be made
in Ohio.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:19.790
The difference is Ohio's only 18 electoral
votes, whereas Florida's twenty nine.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:29.170
So if Biden flips Ohio, but not Florida, he's
still likely needs Ohio plus two, unless it's

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:33.439
a very high population state with more electoral
votes.

00:02:33.439 --> 00:02:37.129
Now, in the end, we've got 50 elections.

00:02:37.129 --> 00:02:41.260
We can't control anything other than our one
vote and we have to make sure to use it.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.989
So when I look at these scenarios, you know,
every once in a while I will look at 270 to

00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:45.989
win.

00:02:45.989 --> 00:02:50.840
Dot com is a great place where you can start
with the 2016 map and say, okay, we start

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:53.799
with 2016 and flip this or flip that.

00:02:53.799 --> 00:02:56.989
There's a bunch of different scenarios that
have Biden winning.

00:02:56.989 --> 00:02:59.140
There's one scenario that has a tie.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:03.719
I believe it's 269 269 and a bunch of scenarios
that have Trump winning.

00:03:03.719 --> 00:03:04.840
All I can do is vote.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:10.190
And so when I cast my ballot via absentee,
which I've already requested in the state

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:15.790
of Massachusetts, I will be doing it with
the belief that.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.810
This state could come down to my vote.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:21.140
It is mathematically unlikely to be that way.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.379
But every single one of us should say.

00:03:23.379 --> 00:03:26.510
Would I vote if my vote could be the difference
maker?

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:30.810
Of course, your vote could be the difference
maker, meaning, yes, you should vote.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.299
And we all need to make sure that we do

